=2 Walkthrough
* Head to {z:Ru'Lude Gardens} and speak with {n:Pherimociel} at (G-6) in the palace for a cutscene which begins this mission.
* You must now complete each of the three Promyvions, which can be done in any order.
** The walkthrough for completing each Promyvion is located in the next mission, {M:The Mothercrystals|The Mothercrystals|The Mothercrystals}.
* **(Optional)** Speak with {n:Rainhard}, {z:Ru'Lude Gardens} (H-6), at the top of the stairs in the palace for some dialogue about {p:Harith}.
* **(Optional)** Speak with {p:Harith} in the Duke's house (H-5) to learn a little more (very little) about the Emptiness.

=2 Notes
You are now able to enter any of the three Promyvion areas. They are accessed by examining the {p:Shattered Telepoint} at the crags in {z:Konschtat Highlands} ({z:Promyvion - Dem}), {z:Tahrongi Canyon} ({z:Promyvion - Mea}), and {z:La Theine Plateau} ({z:Promyvion - Holla}).{br} After examining the {p:Shattered Telepoint} and entering the {z:Hall of Transference}, click on the __Large Apparatus__ to your left to enter Promyvion if this is your first time here. If not, you can enter via the Cermet gate in the center.
* The three Promyvions can be completed in any order.

Some monsters inside Promyvion will drop an item called a "Recollection of..." These items can be traded to {p:Harith} in {z:Ru'Lude Gardens} at (H-5) along with 2,000 gil to receive an Anima. Which can be used to weaken the bosses inside Promyvion if you do them at lower levels as the fights were originally for a party of level 30 players. You may wish to try to obtain a few animas before attempting the bosses, although it is completely optional.
* Just remember not to erase your memory at the __Large Apparatus__ before returning to {p:Harith}.

